# Docker smoke test before commit

After significant changes (backend, frontends, Dockerfiles, compose, nginx, entrypoint, migrations, env), run:

```
./docker/test.sh
```

Do this before telling the user the work is ready to commit. If the script fails, fix the issue and re-run until it passes.

Skip for docs-only or comment-only edits, or when the user asks not to. The test stack is isolated (project `docker-hrd-system-test`, volume `hrd-system-db-test`) and does not touch a live `./deploy.sh` database.
